@*
    Overview of the three kinds of work, framed as a portfolio index rather than a pitch.
    The pain-point hooks and the CTA are gone: each entry says what the work is and what
    backs it, then links to the detail page. Copy is Scott's to sharpen.

    Order is deliberate: nopCommerce first (best proof), .NET second (deepest experience),
    websites last (least backed, so it claims least).
*@

<section class="section--lede">
    <div class="container">
        <p class="topper">What I do</p>
        <h1 class="header">The kinds of projects I work on</h1>
        <p class="text lede__text">
            Three areas, all of it real development on systems people depend on. Each one
            links to what I've built in it.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section>
    <div class="container">
        <ul class="services">
            <li class="service">
                <h2 class="service__title">nopCommerce development</h2>
                <p class="service__text">
                    Custom plugins, integrations, version upgrades and fixes on live stores.
                    I worked on nopCommerce inside agencies, I'm a certified nopCommerce
                    developer, and I run my own platform built on it.
                </p>
                <a class="service__link" asp-controller="Services" asp-action="NopCommerce">
                    nopCommerce development
                </a>
            </li>

            <li class="service">
                <h2 class="service__title">.NET application development</h2>
                <p class="service__text">
                    Maintenance, fixes, new features and integrations on existing .NET systems,
                    plus new builds. The back end, not just the front. I've been doing this
                    since 2005.
                </p>
                <a class="service__link" asp-controller="Services" asp-action="DotNet">
                    .NET application development
                </a>
            </li>

            <li class="service">
                <h2 class="service__title">Business websites</h2>
                <p class="service__text">
                    Fast, server-rendered sites that search engines can read without running
                    JavaScript. This site is one of them.
                </p>
                <a class="service__link" asp-controller="Services" asp-action="SmallBusiness">
                    Business websites
                </a>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>
